  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The diff removes on.pull_request.paths, so the workflow now runs on every PR. The first step (id: changes) lists the PR's changed files with `gh api --paginate` and writes site=true or site=false to GITHUB_OUTPUT. The only real work step is gated on `steps.changes.outputs.site == 'true'`, so on a docs-only PR that step is skipped and the job still finishes successfully. It also handles the details well: it reads the PR number from GITHUB_EVENT_PATH instead of interpolating it into the script, uses a here-string to avoid a SIGPIPE race under pipefail, and grants the pull-requests: read permission the files API needs. Small deductions: the change is untested, and calling the API adds a network dependency (a git diff against the base would also work). The agent says plainly that it did not test it."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Every edit is limited to the trigger, the detect step and the gate. The permissions block is needed for the API call and is least-privilege. The explanatory comment is relevant. The placeholder echo step is kept as is, there is no concurrency group, and nothing was committed. There are no unrelated edits."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 9.0
  },
